  "details": "With a need to prep changes for new builds in advance of release, *cough*Unity2022*cough*, it'd be useful if we could have some kind of in-game Udon value to know if a player is on a beta build and toggle code accordingly.\n\nMy personal usecase is camera offsets have changed in beta, so it'd be real useful in the interim to be able to have alternate code to calculate appropriate camera positioning based on which version the player is using.  (Eg if player.beta == true, use Script A, otherwise use Script B).",
